  "section_notes": "The final S2 allows Ember-type models above 5% to avoid sales stops for up to 24 months with no interim cap and no public per-model disclosure, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 sets an immediate mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, so Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) would be recalled and stopped from sale on entry into force, the largest cost to Halcyon. S1 is strong and uniform (24-hour initial reports for all thermal incidents), and S3 (6-year retrofit) and S4 (36-month suppression) sit inside the acceptable ranges."
